  "question": {
    "text": "The minimum value of $f(x)=e^{\\left(x^4-x^3+x^2\\right)}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "e",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{e}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "-1",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $f(x)=e^{\\left(x^4-x^3+x^2\\right)}, f^{\\prime}(x)=e^{x^4-x^3+x^2}$\n$e^{x^4-x^3+x^2}\\left(4 x^3-3 x^2+2 x\\right) x\\left(4 x^2-3 x+2\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow f(x)$ is decreasing for $x < 0$, increasing for $x>0$\n$\\therefore$ Minimum is at $\\mathrm{x}=0 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{f}(0)=\\mathrm{e}^0=1$"
  }
}